     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, 15 Dec 2021 at 14:27, Ícaro Agostino &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">icaroa...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Simmer developers,</div><div><br></div>Is there an easy way to calculate the individual waiting time (time spent in a queue) for a specific entity at a specific step in the simulation?<br><br><div>Using the <b>get_mo</b>n functions, I couldn&#39;t find an easy solution.</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>Yes, there is. get_mon_arrivals(env, per_resource=TRUE) gives you statistics per arrival and resource. From this dataframe, waiting time is calculated as end_time - start_time - activity_time.</div><div><br></div><div>Iñaki</div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
